An agent manager for agents: one typed control plane for durable agent runs and terminals across your machines, with human inspection and takeover when useful.

Usage:
  wt [flags]
  wt [command]

Available Commands:
  agent        Manage agent adapters
  attach       Attach this terminal to a running egg session
  channel      Show executable channel, isolated state, and update feed
  completion   Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  conversation Inspect persistent parent and child conversations
  daemon       Run this machine’s wing, locally or through a relay
  doctor       Check available agents, embedders, and API keys
  embed        Generate embeddings
  help         Help about any command
  init         Initialize ~/.wingthing directory
  keygen       Generate a JWT signing key (EC P-256)
  local-cert   Manage the on-demand localhost HTTPS certificate
  log          Show task log events
  login        Authenticate this device with the roost
  logout       Remove device authentication
  mcp          Expose Wingthing to LLM clients
  phone        Set up the phone app
  prompt       Manage named, versioned prompt templates
  relay        Start the relay server (web UI + WebSocket relay)
  remote       Manage configured SSH remotes
  retry        Retry a failed task
  roost        Run relay + wing in a single process (self-hosted mode)
  run          Run a prompt or skill
  sandbox      Run an agent in a sandboxed session
  schedule     Manage recurring tasks
  session      Inspect and automate persistent terminal sessions
  start        Start the daemon (alias for wt wing start / wt daemon start)
  status       Task counts and token usage
  stop         Stop the daemon (alias for wt wing stop / wt daemon stop)
  support      Collect diagnostic bundle for troubleshooting
  terminal     Start a persistent shell or command
  thread       Print today's daily thread
  timeline     Show upcoming and recent tasks
  tool-list    List available privileged tools
  update       Update wt to the latest release
  whoami       Show the currently logged-in user
  wings        Find online wings available through a roost

Flags:
  -h, --help                   help for wt
  -r, --remote string          run a supported command on this SSH host or alias
      --remote-binary string   channel-matching executable or absolute path on the remote host (default "wt")
      --remote-cwd string      remote working directory for bare interactive entry
      --remote-state string    absolute state directory on the remote host (sets WINGTHING_DIR and WINGTHING_PREVIEW_DIR there)
  -v, --version                version for wt

Use "wt [command] --help" for more information about a command.
